c","forks":4359,"open_issues":1818,"watchers":24886,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/pulls/12999","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/pull/12999","diff_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/pull/12999.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/pull/12999.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"This isolates the Bazel coverage runner's version of Guava from the\r\nuser's.\r\n\r\nResolves #12998\r\n\r\nTesting Done:\r\n- Verified `bazel coverage` worked against a crufty internal target\r\n  using this patch with java_tools javac11-10.5 and Bazel 4.0.0.\r\n- `bazelisk build src:java_tools.zip`; manual inspection of\r\n  `JacocoCoverage_jarjar_deploy.jar`.\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/12999/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/12999/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":4401904327,"node_id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50NDQwMTkwNDMyNw==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/events/4401904327","actor":{"login":"bazel-io","id":15028808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io","html_url":"https://github.com/bazel-io","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"closed","commit_id":"ce7afe730d90346cf2a67861e6af2fc4462352a5","commit_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/commits/ce7afe730d90346cf2a67861e6af2fc4462352a5","created_at":"2021-03-03T13:05:08Z","state_reason":null,"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/1179117600","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/12998#issuecomment-1179117600","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/12998","id":1179117600,"node_id":"IC_kwDOATz7jc5GR-gg","user":{"login":"JaimeLotero","id":8250309,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyNTAzMDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8250309?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaimeLotero","html_url":"https://github.com/JaimeLotero","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaimeLotero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaimeLotero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaimeLotero/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaimeLotero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaimeLotero/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaimeLotero/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaimeLotero/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaimeLotero/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaimeLotero/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-08T15:30:00Z","updated_at":"2022-07-08T15:30:00Z","body":"> Following appears to have done the trick. `bazel coverage //mycruftytarget` now succeeds and produces a `coverage.dat` usable with `lcov`.\r\n> \r\n> ```diff\r\n> diff --git a/src/java_tools/junitrunner/java/com/google/testing/coverage/JacocoCoverage.jarjar b/src/java_tools/junitrunner/java/com/google/testing/coverage/JacocoCoverage.jarjar\r\n> index 56190d874c..081c5420f8 100644\r\n> --- a/src/java_tools/junitrunner/java/com/google/testing/coverage/JacocoCoverage.jarjar\r\n> +++ b/src/java_tools/junitrunner/java/com/google/testing/coverage/JacocoCoverage.jarjar\r\n> @@ -1,2 +1,3 @@\r\n> +rule com.google.common.** com.google.testing.coverage.jarjar.@0\r\n>  rule org.apache.commons.** com.google.testing.coverage.jarjar.@0\r\n>  rule org.objectweb.asm.** com.google.testing.coverage.jarjar.@0\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nSorry to revive this old issue but I can't find this information anywhere else. I'm getting this exact problem in one huge Java repository; I noticed this patch made it into Bazel 5, but unfortunately I'm using version 4.2.2 and upgrading is not an option for now. How did you test this in-place? Is there any way I can configure Bazel to forcefully introduce this patch to Jacoco?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/1179117600/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"JaimeLotero","id":8250309,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyNTAzMDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8250309?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaimeLotero","html_url":"https://github.com/JaimeLotero","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaimeLotero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaimeLotero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaimeLotero/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaimeLotero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaimeLotero/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaimeLotero/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaimeLotero/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaimeLotero/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaimeLotero/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/1179195666","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/12998#issuecomment-1179195666","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/12998","id":1179195666,"node_id":"IC_kwDOATz7jc5GSRkS","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-08T17:00:41Z","updated_at":"2022-07-08T17:00:41Z","body":"> How did you test this in-place? Is there any way I can configure Bazel to forcefully introduce this patch to Jacoco?\r\n\r\n@JaimeLotero We build java_tools from source.\r\n\r\n1. Determine which java_tools release corresponds to your Bazel version. It looks like Bazel 4.2.2 uses [java_tools 10.6](https://github.com/bazelbuild/java_tools/releases/tag/javac11_v10.6). (See [jdk.WORKSPACE](https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/blob/15371720ae0c40ffc97b74c871d1b38851ef6410/src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/bazel/rules/java/jdk.WORKSPACE).)\r\n2. Download a java_tools release artifact (e.g. [java_tools_javac11_linux-v10.6.zip](https://github.com/bazelbuild/java_tools/releases/download/javac11_v10.6/java_tools_javac11_linux-v10.6.zip)) and extract README.md.\r\n3. Follow instructions from the README to build java_tools.\r\n4. Publish your own java_tools artifacts within your organization.\r\n5. Update your local WORKSPACE to provide its own explicit `http_archive(name = \"remote_java_tools_<platform>\", ...)` repository rules which point to your modified java_tools artifacts.\r\n\r\nHope this helps.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/1179195666/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":6961582623,"node_id":"MEE_lADOATz7jc4wEkW5zwAAAAGe8VIf","url":"https://api.github.c